WEBVTT

00:06.120 --> 00:09.750
Hand over the gold, or the girl gets it!

00:11.410 --> 00:15.700
Rather than gold, what a no-good outlaw like you
deserves is a whole lotta lead.

00:18.250 --> 00:19.830
How cool!

00:20.500 --> 00:22.370
He's so cool!

00:25.040 --> 00:29.410
Rather than gold, what a no-good outlaw like you
deserves is a whole lotta lead.

00:29.410 --> 00:30.910
A lot of what?

00:31.450 --> 00:32.950
M-Mom!

00:33.290 --> 00:36.910
Oh, it's a movie? You like these sorts of films?

00:37.750 --> 00:41.000
Not at all! It was on when I turned on the TV...

00:41.290 --> 00:45.120
So, it's not as if I "like" this kind of thing... I think.

00:45.410 --> 00:49.120
All these guns and killing? That's no good.

00:49.950 --> 00:51.540
Come now, let's get to bed.

00:51.950 --> 00:53.370
Okay...

00:56.410 --> 00:57.830
Asuka-chan?

00:58.500 --> 01:01.660
Oh, sorry, Grandma! Should I turn it down?

01:01.870 --> 01:03.370
No, you're all right.

01:03.370 --> 01:07.370
I think there's someone out in the shed...

01:07.750 --> 01:08.750
Huh?

01:13.080 --> 01:17.910
So, they thought they'd come steal from us
when my family's not around, huh? Cowards!

01:19.500 --> 01:20.870
Hey!

01:20.870 --> 01:22.620
You're in big trouble!

01:23.700 --> 01:24.580
Wait...

02:59.080 --> 03:02.160
And so, allow me to once again introduce...

03:02.160 --> 03:06.040
Seriouska, or should I say, Burglasuka!

03:06.040 --> 03:08.120
I-I said I was sorry!

03:08.370 --> 03:11.790
Stealing is wrong! It's against the law! Don't do it!

03:11.790 --> 03:15.250
You could've just asked for miso!
I would've given you some!

03:15.540 --> 03:17.750
I couldn't help it. Once I smelled it...

03:17.750 --> 03:20.660
It's times like these when you realize
she really is Asuka.

03:20.660 --> 03:23.660
Guess it really is in her blood, in a way.

03:23.870 --> 03:26.910
Still, you showed up way earlier
than we were expecting you.

03:26.910 --> 03:30.660
Well... I wanted to give you your underwear back.

03:31.370 --> 03:32.830
Don't show it to everyone!

03:33.290 --> 03:37.040
There was that, and I had something for Nana.

03:37.040 --> 03:38.160
Huh? For me?

03:38.750 --> 03:40.330
Wait, is this...?

03:40.330 --> 03:42.080
An Astral Module.

03:42.540 --> 03:49.370
Those who have become Equalizers can call out
their Astral Twin and identify with it using this device.

03:49.370 --> 03:52.160
So basically, it's a transformation device?

03:52.160 --> 03:54.200
Well, sure.

03:54.500 --> 03:57.910
Nana's an Equalizer now, so she can use it.

03:58.290 --> 04:00.790
Only Nana can use it? Aww, man...

04:01.120 --> 04:02.700
That's so cool.

04:04.290 --> 04:10.950
Wait, does this mean that you want me
to help out the next time you're in trouble?

04:10.950 --> 04:12.870
No. Don't let this get to your head.

04:12.870 --> 04:15.200
Way to shoot a girl down!

04:15.410 --> 04:19.410
The only time you should use it is in the very rare case
that a Clutter appears in your immediate vicinity.

04:19.910 --> 04:24.660
It's set so you can only use it when it receives
signals from a Clutter in this world.

04:26.580 --> 04:31.040
I've got a signal from a Clutter
in another Fragment. I've got to go.

04:31.040 --> 04:32.450
Wait, already?

04:32.660 --> 04:35.410
I'll likely return sometime. Goodbye for now.

04:39.540 --> 04:42.750
Which means she'll be back
when she runs out of miso, huh?

04:42.750 --> 04:43.950
Yeah, that's it.

04:43.950 --> 04:47.450
Next up, we've got a request from radio name
"Lovey-Dovey Asuka-san."

04:47.950 --> 04:51.200
Her message is "Let's go West!"

04:51.500 --> 04:53.580
Perhaps she's shouting that to the twilight sun?

04:51.700 --> 04:53.160
Lovey-Dovey Asuka?

04:53.160 --> 04:54.950
"Let's go West"?

04:53.580 --> 04:54.950
Oh, to be young again...

04:55.080 --> 04:56.540
That was your request?

04:56.540 --> 04:59.410
Nope, my radio name's "Chikuwasuka."

04:59.540 --> 05:01.250
That could be...

05:03.410 --> 05:06.200
"Let's go West" sounds like the numbers...

05:08.160 --> 05:09.370
It's a frequency!

05:17.290 --> 05:19.870
Sheesh, Asuka-chan, you didn't
have to pull a stunt like this.

05:19.870 --> 05:23.000
You can just tell us what frequency
you want us to use.

05:23.000 --> 05:26.450
Right? I can be a real handful sometimes, huh?

05:26.450 --> 05:28.330
Frequency all set.

05:28.330 --> 05:29.620
Thank you.

05:30.580 --> 05:32.410
Hey, Asuka, you sure you want to do it?

05:33.040 --> 05:35.200
Remember what the other Asuka said?

05:35.200 --> 05:38.700
How when we go to other Fragments,
someone has to be the link?

05:38.950 --> 05:44.410
You end up merging with your otherworld self,
like with what happened to Nana-senpai last time.

05:44.750 --> 05:46.910
I've had enough for one lifetime.

05:46.910 --> 05:51.330
She said it happened to the first person
to move into the other world.

05:51.620 --> 05:56.410
And usually, that means it's the person
wearing the headphones, right?

05:57.950 --> 06:00.250
I'm fine! It could be fun.

06:00.250 --> 06:05.250
If we get split up, let's meet at
the Octave Café in the other world!

06:11.370 --> 06:14.830
Hear us, gathering travelers from distant space-time...

06:15.120 --> 06:18.620
Hear us, warden of the barrier
where day and night mingle...

06:18.790 --> 06:22.290
We are masters of space, but servants of time...

06:22.580 --> 06:26.660
We humbly ask you to show us the way
to a path unlike the one we know...

06:26.660 --> 06:31.200
Take us to the space that sleeps within the twilight.

06:55.750 --> 06:56.540
Huh?!

06:57.830 --> 07:00.450
My clothes changed.

07:00.830 --> 07:03.830
I'm the link!

07:03.830 --> 07:05.950
And, wait, is this world a...?

07:09.540 --> 07:12.160
Oooh! It's a Western!

07:12.160 --> 07:15.750
Once again, we're in a world that looks
very different from our own.

07:16.160 --> 07:20.290
What possibility lead to a world that's this different...

07:20.790 --> 07:24.620
It's just like America around the time of Ii Naosuke, huh?

07:26.950 --> 07:30.080
This looks like it's this world's Octave.

07:30.080 --> 07:33.410
If I wait here, the other senpais should find me...

07:33.410 --> 07:36.750
So, them varmints really haven't come 'round this way?

07:36.750 --> 07:38.790
Why're you askin' again? I'm sure of it.

07:39.040 --> 07:42.200
This here saloon's safe as can be.
Sheriffs come by often.

07:42.200 --> 07:44.620
Why the hell would two wanted women
come here anyway?

07:44.620 --> 07:47.080
A bounty hunter like you should take
one look at this place and know that.

07:47.500 --> 07:51.200
Sometimes, reality ain't much like
what it appears to be.

07:51.200 --> 07:52.290
But all right.

07:52.290 --> 07:55.290
I believe you, sweetheart.

07:56.330 --> 07:59.700
It looks like the Asuka-senpai and Yu-senpai
in this world never even knew each other,

07:59.700 --> 08:02.580
let alone been childhood friends.

08:02.580 --> 08:05.120
What does that make Nana-senpai and Chloe-senpai?

08:07.750 --> 08:09.040
Hey, now!

08:12.250 --> 08:15.080
Just you wait. I'll catch you two rascals yet.

08:16.810 --> 08:18.660
WANTED
DEAD OR ALIVE

08:17.080 --> 08:19.080
Huh?! Wanted?!

08:18.950 --> 08:20.450
Crime: Bank Robbery
Reward:

08:19.080 --> 08:20.450
Bank robbery?!

08:20.620 --> 08:22.540
This is seriously freaky...

08:22.540 --> 08:25.080
Oh, I turned into Nana-senpai for a second...

08:28.540 --> 08:31.870
Man, this really feels like an old Western film.

08:31.870 --> 08:33.830
Look, look, a horse!

08:34.870 --> 08:37.790
They've got cars and motorcycles too, though.

08:37.790 --> 08:40.080
I saw people using cell phones, too.

08:40.080 --> 08:43.330
Ours... don't work, of course.

08:43.330 --> 08:46.450
It feels like we're in that Akeyuki Western Village place.

08:46.450 --> 08:50.410
Okay, once we're all together,
let's set out and see the sights!

08:51.580 --> 08:52.830
What's that ruckus about?

08:52.830 --> 08:55.620
Some woman's husband and lover
are havin' themselves a duel.

08:56.080 --> 08:59.330
Somehow, I don't think this is a touristy place...

08:59.620 --> 09:00.620
Yeah...

09:03.290 --> 09:05.540
You no-good, four-flushin' cheat!

09:05.540 --> 09:06.750
Yaji-sensei?!

09:07.500 --> 09:10.000
Why would I have to cheat?

09:10.000 --> 09:15.200
I have it all: looks, money,
and poker skill to boot. Unlike you.

09:15.200 --> 09:17.330
Don't matter how good you look!

09:15.830 --> 09:17.870
I've seen that guy before!

09:17.330 --> 09:18.700
Doesn't keep you from being a dirty, rotten cheater!

09:18.160 --> 09:20.290
Hey, go get them to knock it off, yeah?

09:18.700 --> 09:21.160
Please. With my good looks,

09:21.160 --> 09:22.910
That's your job, ain't it?

09:21.160 --> 09:23.290
I don't have to resort to cheating.

09:22.910 --> 09:24.910
Huh? My job?

09:23.290 --> 09:27.040
Stop jawin' me to death! There's no way you won
seven times in a row all fair and square!

09:24.910 --> 09:26.540
C'mon, now, git!

09:27.040 --> 09:30.790
Maybe I'm just blessed with good luck,
just like I've been blessed with this handsome face.

09:30.790 --> 09:34.750
U-um, p-please don't fight here.

09:30.790 --> 09:33.700
Looks like you've been lackin' in good fortune
since the day you were born.

09:33.700 --> 09:35.660
You lily-livered varmint! You're dead!

09:34.750 --> 09:38.550
Maybe you can settle this peacefully...

09:35.660 --> 09:37.410
C'mon, let's take this out back!

09:37.410 --> 09:39.620
I'll beat that pretty-boy face of yours into a bloody pulp!

09:39.620 --> 09:41.870
How about you just leave instead?

09:47.080 --> 09:49.450
Sh-Sheriff Hakuma! Aw, hell!

09:53.250 --> 09:55.120
Many thanks, Sher-!

09:55.580 --> 09:58.040
You'd better shape up, too.

09:58.040 --> 10:01.870
I don't much like cheaters hangin' around my town.

10:02.540 --> 10:03.750
Dammit!

10:06.660 --> 10:09.160
I've been lookin' for you, Silverstone.

10:09.160 --> 10:10.160
Come with me.

10:10.160 --> 10:11.080
Huh?!

10:11.200 --> 10:14.410
Stand up straight, now!
You're the sheriff's deputy.

10:14.410 --> 10:17.200
It's up to you to uphold the law in this here town.

10:17.200 --> 10:18.370
Huh...

10:19.410 --> 10:23.410
Wait, I'm... the sheriff's deputy?

10:33.120 --> 10:35.410
See, there is an Octave here!

10:36.410 --> 10:40.290
I've always wanted to go through doors like these!

10:40.290 --> 10:41.790
Hey, it's Yu.

10:41.790 --> 10:42.580
Huh?

10:42.750 --> 10:44.950
Guess she works here...

10:45.370 --> 10:48.620
If she sees me, she'll have lots of questions for us...

10:48.620 --> 10:52.120
I'll wait out here, you guys go look for Mia.

10:52.120 --> 10:53.200
Okay.

10:54.500 --> 10:55.750
Howdy, there!

10:56.080 --> 10:58.410
You again? You're a stubborn little mule, aren't ya?

10:58.410 --> 10:59.120
Huh?

10:59.120 --> 11:01.200
Why don't you go find another saloon to...

11:01.200 --> 11:01.950
Huh?!

11:03.620 --> 11:06.870
You caught those two wanted robbers?

11:06.870 --> 11:08.000
Wh-what?

11:11.370 --> 11:13.660
No way, is that us?!

11:14.750 --> 11:18.450
Wanted, dead or alive...

11:25.660 --> 11:26.870
Please, let us hide here!

11:26.870 --> 11:28.910
She's right on our tail!

11:28.910 --> 11:31.160
Huh? You're those robbers...

11:31.370 --> 11:32.870
Am I seein' double...?

11:33.910 --> 11:36.910
Hey. You saw those two come
runnin' through here, didn't ya?

11:39.830 --> 11:41.040
Where'd they go?!

11:41.040 --> 11:42.620
U-umm...

11:44.080 --> 11:46.750
Hey, now, you're gonna cause me a heap of trouble!

11:48.950 --> 11:51.370
I've finally got you cornered, you no-good bandits!

11:51.370 --> 11:52.450
You better come quietly!

11:53.660 --> 11:54.830
Wait, us?

11:54.830 --> 11:57.040
Hold on, you've got the wrong people.

11:57.540 --> 11:59.500
You shut your mouths, you rotten outlaws!

11:59.500 --> 12:01.370
Oh, crap... Chloe!

12:01.370 --> 12:02.410
Got it!

12:03.620 --> 12:04.450
Hold it!

12:04.450 --> 12:05.750
Wait for me!

12:09.910 --> 12:10.830
Dangit!

12:11.000 --> 12:12.660
You ain't gettin' away this time!

12:12.870 --> 12:13.790
Huh?

12:14.540 --> 12:15.620
What?!

12:18.410 --> 12:20.620
Boy, that there was close!

12:20.620 --> 12:23.410
Why'd she leave, though?

12:23.410 --> 12:25.370
What do you mean, "why"?!

12:25.370 --> 12:28.700
It's your fault my friends had to run off like that!

12:28.700 --> 12:30.080
What am I gonna do?!

12:30.080 --> 12:31.120
What...?

12:31.120 --> 12:33.250
There're two of you bounty hunters?!

12:33.250 --> 12:35.660
No! I'm Chikuwasuka!

12:35.870 --> 12:39.120
Hey, Nana and Chloe just ran off some...

12:48.080 --> 12:50.080
Why are you eating Chikuwa right now?

12:50.080 --> 12:54.580
Look, everything's getting real complicated right now,
so I figured I need to relax a little.

13:03.120 --> 13:07.040
Ugh, I can't do this, there's no way
a trendy girl like me can sprint like that!

13:08.000 --> 13:10.790
Maybe we... gave her the slip.

13:14.910 --> 13:16.580
Yeehaw!

13:24.000 --> 13:26.080
Looks like the Sheriff ain't in.

13:24.010 --> 13:26.080
Closed today due to
a prior engagement.
Please come again tomorrow.
Municipal Sheriff's Office

13:26.250 --> 13:29.500
And here I was hopin' to rope you two in
and get that reward money before sunup.

13:29.500 --> 13:33.450
I told you, we're not wanted criminals, okay?!

13:33.450 --> 13:36.080
What're you jabberin' about?
You look just like them.

13:36.080 --> 13:37.620
Our clothes are totally different!

13:37.620 --> 13:39.160
I'm telling you, you've got the wrong people!

13:39.160 --> 13:41.450
You could change out of clothes.

13:41.450 --> 13:43.160
Geez, Asuka, you're such a blockhead!

13:43.160 --> 13:44.200
Stop struggling!

13:44.910 --> 13:46.830
How'd you know my name?

13:46.830 --> 13:48.250
That's because-

13:48.250 --> 13:52.370
Nope, never mind. I don't have time
to hear out the likes of bandits.

13:54.120 --> 13:56.410
I hate this Asuka!

13:56.660 --> 14:01.540
Looks like Asuka's personality
varies greatly between Fragments.

14:01.750 --> 14:04.370
This Asuka is stubborn and rude.

14:04.370 --> 14:09.580
I don't know who you're comparin' me to,
but you gotta be tough to make it in this world.

14:09.790 --> 14:12.450
The only person who can protect you is yourself.

14:12.870 --> 14:16.040
Everything here's decided by duels, after all.

14:16.830 --> 14:19.500
Everything's decided by duels?!

14:19.500 --> 14:20.830
What the heck?!

14:20.830 --> 14:23.200
I can't believe this world is that uncivilized!

14:23.200 --> 14:26.290
I can't believe you're that surprised about it.

14:26.290 --> 14:29.870
I get it. Looks like we've got no choice
but to believe y'all.

14:29.870 --> 14:32.870
You must really have come from another world.

14:32.870 --> 14:36.700
Ah! I knew you'd get it
if we explained it to you, Chloe!

14:36.950 --> 14:39.700
I still only half believe this stuff.

14:39.700 --> 14:41.580
You've got no choice to believe in it now.

14:41.580 --> 14:44.450
When I do, you're gonna say "I win," aren't you?

14:44.450 --> 14:47.500
I won't! I'll just think it!

14:48.330 --> 14:50.660
You guys are pretty funny.

14:50.660 --> 14:52.410
You must be good friends, huh?

14:52.410 --> 14:56.040
That's right! We're really good friends
back in our world!

14:57.370 --> 15:00.080
Now that I'm getting comfortable,
I gotta go to the bathroom.

15:00.080 --> 15:01.540
I'll be right back!

15:01.540 --> 15:02.950
Oh, me too.

15:05.790 --> 15:08.830
I hope Nana and Chloe are okay...

15:08.830 --> 15:12.040
Yeah, I'm worried about them, and Mia, too.

15:12.040 --> 15:13.910
Where is she?

15:15.160 --> 15:18.370
Hey, you thinkin' what I'm thinkin'?

15:18.750 --> 15:22.620
Yeah. You think with those two...

15:35.080 --> 15:37.910
Man, this ain't interesting in the least.

15:37.910 --> 15:39.660
No one here's watchin', either.

15:39.910 --> 15:45.660
Judge Hiishi's trials are usually interesting,
but lately they're right boring.

15:46.000 --> 15:50.500
Guess this year she'll have to give up her seat
as the most popular judge.

15:58.450 --> 16:04.330
In the land ownership duel between
Eita Mobukawa and Biigo Zakoshima...

16:04.330 --> 16:06.700
I hereby declare Eita Mobukawa the victor.

16:06.700 --> 16:08.330
That is all for today.

16:09.830 --> 16:13.080
That was awful. I can't believe that's a fair trial...

16:13.410 --> 16:16.080
You're soundin' like a real greenhorn there.

16:16.080 --> 16:17.950
This is just how the world is.

16:24.120 --> 16:29.500
But if everything can be decided by duels,
what do they need sheriffs for?

16:29.500 --> 16:32.950
Duels are fundamentally for civil disputes.

16:33.290 --> 16:37.250
If there's clear evidence that
someone committed a crime,

16:37.250 --> 16:40.000
you can charge them guilty without a duel.

16:40.330 --> 16:44.040
It's the sheriff's job to find that evidence.

16:44.620 --> 16:45.450
In a word...

16:45.450 --> 16:47.410
My, if it isn't Sheriff Hakuma.

16:49.790 --> 16:52.500
Judge Hiishi. Need something from me?

16:52.830 --> 16:54.700
No, just saying hello.

16:55.450 --> 16:57.370
That your new deputy?

16:57.500 --> 16:58.580
That's right.

16:58.580 --> 17:02.250
I-I'm Mia Silverstone! Pleased to meet you!

17:02.250 --> 17:04.200
Young and cute to boot...

17:04.580 --> 17:07.040
Just what we need to keep this town safe.

17:07.040 --> 17:08.700
Right, Sheriff?

17:09.540 --> 17:10.910
Excuse me.

17:20.410 --> 17:23.250
U-um, Sheriff Hakuma?

17:23.250 --> 17:24.410
It's our job.

17:24.410 --> 17:25.160
Huh?

17:25.580 --> 17:32.290
Some judge who only cares about attractin'
audience members can't deliver any true justice.

17:33.040 --> 17:35.700
We're the only ones who can.

17:37.330 --> 17:39.830
That's why you've gotta be strong, Silverstone.

17:41.910 --> 17:47.040
Find the strength to stand up to
any kind of violence, any kind of injustice.

17:47.040 --> 17:49.580
Without that, you won't be able to do your job.

17:50.370 --> 17:54.080
But, I'm not really that strong at all...

18:03.000 --> 18:04.040
Eat.

18:04.040 --> 18:05.700
Here's your dinner.

18:05.700 --> 18:08.080
This kind of thing makes you realize
she really is Asuka.

18:08.080 --> 18:09.950
It's in her blood.

18:09.950 --> 18:11.080
Thanks.

18:11.080 --> 18:12.330
Yeah, thanks.

18:20.700 --> 18:24.700
Hey, Asuka, why're you a bounty hunter?

18:24.910 --> 18:26.870
Why're you asking me that?

18:26.870 --> 18:29.750
I mean, I know how the world is and all,

18:29.750 --> 18:32.580
but don't you think there's another job
that fits you better?

18:34.290 --> 18:39.910
Ain't many jobs a girl can get when she's 15
and her parents have already passed.

18:42.000 --> 18:45.200
Did you lose your parents in a duel...?

18:48.330 --> 18:51.910
I got no obligation to tell that to the likes of you.

18:54.870 --> 18:56.700
She's so annoying.

19:02.370 --> 19:04.120
I'm back.

19:04.580 --> 19:07.040
Welcome back, Mia!

19:07.040 --> 19:08.500
Mom...

19:09.040 --> 19:12.200
Thank goodness. My mom's still here.

19:13.450 --> 19:15.750
You must've had a tough day at work today, huh?

19:15.750 --> 19:17.040
Good work out there.

19:17.040 --> 19:17.950
Thanks.

19:17.950 --> 19:20.540
But don't you go getting weak on me, all right?

19:20.540 --> 19:24.790
Especially after you were so stubborn with me about
wanting that job, even when I was so against it.

19:24.790 --> 19:25.870
Huh?

19:25.870 --> 19:26.870
I was?

19:26.870 --> 19:28.700
My, you don't need to play dumb with me.

19:28.700 --> 19:32.200
You wanted to change the world
so the weak would have a chance, right?

19:32.200 --> 19:34.450
I was so touched by your passion!

19:34.450 --> 19:38.160
Especially when you said,
"I want to be a hero of justice for this town!"

19:38.160 --> 19:40.580
I said that?

19:40.910 --> 19:43.000
Come now, go hop in the bath.

19:46.700 --> 19:49.500
You should be safe and sound here.

19:49.830 --> 19:51.290
Thanks a lot.

19:54.200 --> 19:56.910
We found a place to sleep for tonight!

19:56.910 --> 20:01.370
Oh, but there's a group of people sleepin'
the next room over, so try to keep it down, all right?

20:01.540 --> 20:02.830
Huh?

20:02.830 --> 20:08.080
We're actually lookin' after a bunch of kids
who don't have families to go back to.

20:08.080 --> 20:09.660
Wow, really...?

20:09.660 --> 20:13.500
People are dyin' left and right from duels in this world.

20:13.500 --> 20:16.410
There're lots of kids out there who
find themselves all on their lonesome.

20:16.410 --> 20:20.040
Someone's gotta look after them, right?

20:20.040 --> 20:21.410
Yeah...

20:21.910 --> 20:26.330
Wait, is that why you've been robbing banks?

20:26.330 --> 20:28.290
Come on, that can't be why.

20:30.120 --> 20:31.080
It is?!

20:31.500 --> 20:35.330
Yeah, well... I guess you could put it that way.

20:35.330 --> 20:39.040
Anyway, since we're on the subject of it and all...

20:39.200 --> 20:42.500
Truth is, we're plannin' another one for tomorrow.

20:42.500 --> 20:44.040
You girls wanna help?

20:44.040 --> 20:44.750
What?

20:44.750 --> 20:45.750
Help with what?

20:45.750 --> 20:47.160
Robbin' a bank!

20:47.160 --> 20:50.370
C'mon, we're friends now, ain't we?

20:50.370 --> 20:53.950
It's hard to rob a bank when it's just the two of us.

20:53.950 --> 20:55.580
With four of us, though...

20:55.580 --> 20:56.700
Wait, wait, wait!

20:56.700 --> 21:00.500
Don't try to make it sound like you're
a soccer team who's just two people short!

21:00.500 --> 21:01.660
Y-yeah!

21:02.040 --> 21:06.120
I can understand where you're coming from,
but stealing is a crime! I won't do it!

21:06.120 --> 21:09.540
Aww, really? You seem like you
could totally do it, though.

21:09.540 --> 21:11.620
I totally couldn't!

21:11.620 --> 21:15.950
I, Asuka Tsuichimiya, am a woman of common sense!

21:19.330 --> 21:20.870
What?! Who're you?!

21:21.370 --> 21:22.580
Hi!

21:22.580 --> 21:23.580
Huh?!

21:25.120 --> 21:30.120
Radio name "Lovey-Dovey Asuka," Yu-chan here!

21:30.120 --> 21:31.580
Me again?!

21:31.580 --> 21:35.290
Hey, Asuka, let's go rob a bank.

21:35.290 --> 21:37.120
C'mon!

21:41.750 --> 21:43.700
Welcome to Good Night Dream.

21:45.120 --> 21:49.540
Tonight, we'll be bringing you some
lovely music to enjoy under the stars...

21:50.660 --> 21:53.330
The hero of justice for this town...

21:57.660 --> 22:01.700
Well, it's only till I have to go back to my world.

22:02.620 --> 22:05.120
I'll do my best to be a good Sheriff's Deputy!

22:05.790 --> 22:09.120
Just so I can get a little bit stronger!
